---
import ArticleLayout from '../layouts/ArticleLayout.astro';
import NewsletterEmbed from '../components/NewsletterEmbed.astro';
---
<ArticleLayout
    title="Leaving Lucis — Max Guerois"
    description="A few months ago, I decided to step away from Lucis, the company I co-founded. A note on what we built, and what comes next."
    ogUrl="https://maxguerois.com/lucis-chapter"
    ogImage="https://maxguerois.com/health-journey/og/lucis-chapter.jpg"
>

<div class="container">
    <a href="/" class="back">← Back home</a>

    <div class="article-meta">June 9, 2026</div>
    <h1 class="article-title">Leaving Lucis</h1>

    <img
        class="article-img"
        src="/health-journey/lucis-chapter.jpg"
        alt="Max speaking to the Zero Club community at a meetup"
        loading="lazy"
    >

    <div class="article-body">

        <p>A few months ago, I decided to step away from Lucis, the company I co-founded.</p>

        <p>Lucis grew out of a personal obsession with health. How to optimize it. How to measure it. How to actually take control of it. (I've been writing about this <a href="/newsletter">here</a>.)</p>

        <div style="margin: 40px 0;">
            <NewsletterEmbed />
        </div>

        <p>It started in a WhatsApp group. A handful of people in Europe, deep into longevity, trying to understand their bloodwork and what to do with it. We kept running into the same problem: if you wanted to take your health seriously in Europe, you still had to stitch too much together on your own.</p>

        <p>That obsession became a community.</p>

        <p>That community became a company.</p>

        <p>Y Combinator backed the vision.</p>

        <p>Lucis grew into one of Europe's leading preventive health platforms, reached thousands of people, and became the kind of company ambitious people wanted to throw themselves into.</p>

        <p>I'm proud of what we built, grateful for everyone who believed in it, and still deeply convinced that preventive, personalized health is the future of medicine in Europe.</p>

        <p>Leaving something you helped build is never easy.</p>

        <p>Maxime Berthelot and Baptiste Debever have poured everything into this company. I trust where they're taking it. I'll be rooting for them every step of the way.</p>

        <p>Next for me: I'm going back to what I love most. Starting from a problem that matters, finding the right people, and building something from the ground up.</p>

        <p>Lucis taught me a lot. And I've never been more excited about what comes next.</p>

    </div>

    <div class="article-footer">
        <span class="author-line">By <a href="/">Max Guerois</a></span>
    </div>

    <!-- Newsletter CTA -->
    <div style="margin-top: 48px;">
        <NewsletterEmbed />
    </div>
</div>
</ArticleLayout>
